# Plan Mode — workspace extension (cursor-sdk)

Parent rule: `../.cursor/rules/plan-mode.mdc` (Cursor IDE Plan mode checklist).
This file adds **cursor-sdk `sdk_mode: plan`** — a distinct but composable
plan-first dispatch path on the SDK substrate.

## Two plan surfaces

| Surface | Mechanism | Output | Land |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Cursor IDE Plan mode** | IDE mode switch + parent `plan-mode.mdc` checklist | `tmp/prompts/{project}/phase{n}.md` | Lead / attended implement |
| **cursor-sdk plan mode** | `sdk_mode: plan` on `team_dispatch(seat=cursor-sdk)` | cortex:// sidecars, specs, reviews | **Forbidden** on plan leg — nest `contract=implement` after |

Do not conflate them: IDE Plan mode is in-seat authoring; cursor-sdk plan is a
headless read-only dispatch (`read_only=true`, lease-exempt) that closes with
`plan:closeout_verdict=PLAN_COMPLETE|PARTIAL`.

## When to use cursor-sdk plan

- Sparse recon / architecture bind before implement (`contract: none|consult|ask|recon|seed`)
- Conductor G3 row before `implement_ready` (`work-item-seed-path` G-row ladder)
- Packet or wire explicitly names `sdk_mode: plan`
- `read_only=true` on plan-default contracts (unless `sdk_mode: agent` overrides)

## When **not** to use cursor-sdk plan

- `implement`, `pure-mechanical`, `conductor` — worker **422** for `sdk_mode=plan`
- Default implement dispatches (omit → `agent`)

## After plan — implement handoff

1. Plan closeout: artifact URIs + `plan:closeout_verdict=PLAN_COMPLETE`
2. Stamp `implement_ready` on todo when densify complete
3. Nest or sibling dispatch: `contract=implement`, `sdk_mode: agent` (or omit),
   `nest_under=<plan_dispatch_id>` when continuing on same worktree

Closeout may carry **`nest_implement_hint`** when `PLAN_COMPLETE` ∧ `implement_ready`
— see `docs/agent-guides/cursor-sdk-conversation-mode.md` § Two-hop plan → implement.

